<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Time of Troubles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1598">1598</a>–<a href="/years/1613">1613</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Time of Troubles was a period of political crisis, famine, civil war and foreign intervention in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> between the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik-dynasty">Rurik dynasty</a> in 1598 and the election of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-of-russia">Michael Romanov</a> as tsar in 1613. Pretenders claiming to be <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a>'s dead son Dmitry won wide support, and Polish-Lithuanian forces occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> from 1610 to 1612, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> seized Novgorod.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/time-of-troubles.jpg" alt="Time of Troubles" width="320" height="376" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Konstantin Makovsky · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Appeal_of_Minin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
